an write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each function.\n\n- I is *not* a surjection. As a counterexample, choose $2\\in {-1,0,1,2,3}.$ There is no number $x\\in {-1,0,1,2}$ such that $f(x)=2.$ The only number $x$ that satisfies $f(x)={x}^{2}-1=2$ is $x=\\sqrt{3},$ but $\\sqrt{3}\\notin {-1,0,1,2}.$\n\n- II is *not* a surjection. As a counterexample, choose $2\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ such that $g(x)=2.$ In fact, $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1$ for all $x\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\n- III is a surjection. Given $y\\in [0,\\infty ),$ choose $x={y}^{2}\\in [0,\\infty ).$ Then $h(x)=h({y}^{2})=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}}=y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362540 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362541 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362542 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362543 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362544 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362542 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362539 1080 #uuid "6a3f5143-83c3-5718-baa2-eb554713414f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362540 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362540 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362540 1084 #uuid "05a3447a-047f-53a1-a1a7-14d0160e224a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362541 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362541 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 tru