corresponds to the vector ${v}_{2}$ such that $(A-3I){v}_{2}={v}_{1}.$\n\nNow, computing $A-3I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]-(3)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix equation $(A-3I){v}_{2}={v}_{1}$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-1-{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get  \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b=(-2)+1=-1.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362623 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362624 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362625 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362626 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362627 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362627 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362622 1080 #uuid "3361f0b5-e38d-57f0-a3df-c0210c05a1e7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362623 1081 "3" 13194139533445 1759218604