083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362696 1084 #uuid "bc9700a5-8075-5cc2-ab61-d44802827f04" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362697 1081 "[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362697 1084 #uuid "be31030c-d727-58ad-89f7-7c11aefdedb8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362699 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1069 "q-112494" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,J=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Given that $A=PJ{P}^{-1}$ is a Jordan canonical decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the second column of the matrix $P?$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,z=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1072 #uuid "87ae16ee-db15-5f83-b8a6-695e01237b18" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1074 "First, notice that the Jordan matrix $J$ consists of one Jordan block $J={J}_{2}(-1).$ \n\nTherefore, the columns of $P$ form the following chain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}_{2}(-1) & : & {v}_{2}\\overset{A-(-1)I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-(-1)I\\,}{\\to }0 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the second column of $P$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to $\\lambda =-1.$ \n\nNow, computing $A-(-1)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]-(-1)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAmong the given vectors, only $y$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2,$ since\n\n$$\n(A-(-1)I)y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=x,\n$$\n\nand, therefore,\n\n$$\n(A-(-1)I)^{2}y=(A-(-1)I)x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\overset{A-(-1)I\\,}{\\to }[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\overset{A-(-1)I\\,}{\\to }0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe other vectors do not satisfy this condition." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362700 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362701 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362702 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362703 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362704 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362701 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1080 #uuid "a9409570-57d3-5e2c-9365-c691fbd3294a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362700 1081 "$z$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362700 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362700 1084 #uuid "41bea20d-c20b-5a8e-90bc-317d76445d96" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362701 1081 "$y$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362701 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362701 1084 #uuid "f5fb3835-f205-50c6-8534-6eee4b2d8bba" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362702 1081 "$y$ and  $z$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362702