wer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362728 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362729 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362730 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362731 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362732 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362729 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1080 #uuid "caef7be4-fa1f-5ecd-8432-0db8e2abf1fb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1084 #uuid "34c119eb-a2e9-5e7b-aece-194690e3575f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362729 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362729 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362729 1084 #uuid "f11bcfb0-554a-553b-a2cd-9d076207bb59" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362730 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362730 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362730 1084 #uuid "7d17c850-0945-5f89-a53a-ffaee5e1a53e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362731 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362731 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362731 1084 #uuid "04ec628e-d678-57c6-afb0-df8af8ce90b1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362732 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362732 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362732 1084 #uuid "649bb3e8-6868-569d-a178-c5ab91222bdf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362733 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362734 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362733 1069 "q-122656" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362733 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362733 1071 "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $M(x,y)=⟨y-{x}^{2},3x+{y}^{2},\\frac{1}{x+y}⟩$\n- $N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$\n- $P(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\sqrt{1-t}\\,⟩$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362733 1072 #uuid "502cb71c-02d6-5e14-a31b-2cee28a0a5ef" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362733 1074 "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $M(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  ${R}^{2}$ to vectors in ${R}^{3}$ (not in ${R}^{2}$).\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $P(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ \n(not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362735 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362736 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362737 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362738 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362739 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362739 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362734 1080 #uuid "21763b78-6aa3-55ed-be0a-c14268a02c40" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362735 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362735 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362735 1084 #uuid "16526cbf-eed9-5dc8-b49d-07c80cc53aee" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362736 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362736 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362736 1084 #uuid "76cc8d11-9c5e-5b66-857e-79223281043f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362737 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362737 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362737 1084 #uuid "1bfe71e4-e268-5307-ad87-4f7d22a6a41f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362738 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362738 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362738 1084 #uuid "85e5e6ca-2257-5462-aa74-7664e109c0ef" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362739 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362739 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362739 1084 #uuid "d3ffeac8-d5ff-53ee-ad33-6d914cd947c0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362741 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362740 1069 "q-122660" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362740 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362740 1071 "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4})\\,i+\\frac{xy}{x-1}\\,j\\,.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362740 1072 #uuid "76ab55a5-b7ae-513b-bef2-54d7a5d78561" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362740 1074 "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4}),\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4=0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}.\n$$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $Q$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4,\\,x\\ne 1}\\,.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362742 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362743 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362744 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362745 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362746 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362744 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362741 1080 #uuid "5ced28f1-8592-507f-b2f3-ca4edef0e463" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362742 1081 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,x\\ne 1}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362742 1083 #edb/ref 1759218