very point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $D(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $E(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ to vectors in ${R}^{3}$ (not ${R}^{2}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362749 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362750 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362751 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362752 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362753 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362752 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362748 1080 #uuid "cee31fa4-3f78-5e6b-b4f0-0888305b3c27" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362749 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362749 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362749 1084 #uuid "d818659d-904f-56ab-a894-ba5c08da4a69" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362750 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362750 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362750 1084 #uuid "073a4146-a75e-5400-a120-20b8b4dcbe03" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362751 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362751 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362751 1084 #uuid "25a00a6a-d7e9-5e03-949c-8562fa76683a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362752 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362752 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362752 1084 #uuid "60870366-832c-58f3-ab71-17ad52ae15cf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362753 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362753 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362753 1084 #uuid "4a72a1c4-87b7-54cc-8c12-34d1ba68b017" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362754 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362755 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362754 1069 "q-122677" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362754 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362754 1071 "Determine which of the following shaded regions depicts the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y-x}}\\,i+\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,j\\,.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362754 1072 #uuid "e932ad34-5aaf-594d-8943-da2547f2acb1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362754 1074 "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y-x}},\\,Q(x,y)=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the radical is positive. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\ny-x>0\\,⟹\\,y>x.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{1},$ shown below:\n\n![](images/c7/c78759bc8f9926159065129e00c1fc8b4341ab83ad40cc87e67a2e82b3e6b089.png)\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the radical is positive or equal to zero. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n2-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{2},$ which is a circle of radius $\\sqrt{2},$ as shown below:\n\n![](images/bd/bdf02ff330f256327d0c9f1147c388b25184610b36ea7ab77bb2c570ec3be19a.png)\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by ${D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2},$ shown below.\n\n![](images/0d/0d3180a60e33c05e904c8fc00fdec4197510198fef3de3fa8c7b3549609205f6.png)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362756 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362757 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362758 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362759 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362760 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362757 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362755 1080 #uuid "ab0fa5e8-8931-50fe-a99e-b67ba6230eec" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362756 1081 "images/59/59ec29347dea9437c8217a208bde0a8b200e37fcbce9c223d0358011a0685297.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362756 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362756 1084 #uuid "1ac4dc2b-7925-5bb6-a8d7-26be528ca51e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1081 "images/27/27f151bdd3d619de0988b786e6b7517a7f7586844f9a7a35bf651063e7a7dfd1.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362757 1084 #uuid "de160c2f-72c8-5594-b423-821d641cf29b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362758 1081 "images/fa/fadd7ae69d155ebf23586b88369da8f6624b1919942dad543917592f2d3c