ent of $(x-1)^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ about $x=1?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362788 1072 #uuid "5c845d02-903c-5c34-8e78-373a4e0abbab" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362788 1074 "The coefficient of $(x-1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt[3]{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-2/3} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{9}{x}^{-5/3} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{10}{27}{x}^{-8/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(1),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-1)=\\frac{10}{27}\\cdot {1}^{-8/3}=\\frac{10}{27}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(1)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{10}{27}=\\frac{5}{81}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x-1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{5}{81}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362790 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362791 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362792 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362793 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362794 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362794 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362789 1080 #uuid "1d2dd421-62cc-5914-be50-e572793cac99" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362790 1081 "\\frac{10}{27}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362790 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362790 1084 #uuid "87249d32-72e3-5606-8b09-a87347fe280a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362791 1081 "-\\frac{5}{27}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362791 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 175921860455