592186362942 1072 #uuid "2a641d94-d436-5610-8401-c196fdb866a7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362942 1074 "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(3{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2})\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}3{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}6{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}3{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-0){\\int }_{-1}^{0}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}{|}_{-1}^{0}) \\\\  & =2({0}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}6{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(0-(-1)){\\int }_{0}^{2}6{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{y}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(3{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=2+16=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362944 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362945 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362946 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362947 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362948 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362948 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362943 1080 #uuid "4f5de000-5e2e-5293-bbbc-fea0dfb73f12" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362944 1081 "16" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362944 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362944 1084 #uuid "a2b5bd46-9ad9-5287-8540-de4fec5b349c" 