86363086 1084 #uuid "9504c561-f825-5c73-ab9f-071939988f76" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363087 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363087 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363087 1084 #uuid "fb5e9db7-bd7d-592b-a932-d8249d8253cb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363088 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363088 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363088 1084 #uuid "ce36cb26-a73b-51ff-8442-c8e214bc0969" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363089 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363090 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363089 1069 "q-132497" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363089 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363089 1071 "![](images/9f/9fb82d3ef2fa47cc67e04ae7c43bb2f0fe021adb73063107f9ad16e9627cc451.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed between the curves $x=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}+1$ and $x={y}^{2}-2,$ above the $x$-axis, as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dA=$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363089 1072 #uuid "808843b5-4ec6-51d5-9767-8d30c84390fc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363089 1074 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. \n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}+1 & ={y}^{2}-2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}{y}^{2}-3 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)(y+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are\n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/9e/9ed5a24f07ad025cbf47d664ac2c9e2f6525e43b0bc73c0b25eb7e3e5c60ac47.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}-2\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363091 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363092 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363093 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363094 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363095 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363094 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363090 1080 #uuid "944e9043-a2b2-5890-9087-b38a43ff9304" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363091 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{2}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363091 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363091 1084 #uuid "81410832-b6b3-5770-a5c8-ab39c78cd75a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363092 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/4+1}^{{y}^{2}-2}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363092 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363092 1084 #uuid "aa8f5140-7e4d-5c07-9a35-b2c5c8c58b49" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363093 1081 "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363093 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363093 1084 #uuid "4a5c0904-845d-5506-b9ed-cbbf441c4201" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363094 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363094 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363094 1084 #uuid "0abdda0e-9501-5f4b-a759-4d62540e6335" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363095 1081 "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363095 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363095 1084 #uuid "3eec9544-9a54-5558-87b3-c7be335e7ad3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363096 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363097 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363096 1069 "q-132516" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363096 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363096 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt{-x}$ and the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+3),$ above the $x$-axis. What is ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA\\,$ expressed as a repeated integral?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363096 1072 #uuid "9c102617-2635-5783-b418-6ddb6be7b181" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363096 1074 "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/c4/c4531d05ef2634d04e590b099ba5ec0269c9c00f12dce82442043cad4377db1a.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=\\sqrt{-x}$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+3)$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{-x} & \\,⟹\\,x=-{y}^{2} \\\\ y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+3) & \\,⟹\\,x=2y-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2} & =2y-3 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2y-3 & =0 \\\\ (y+3)(y-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/31/3187c1520326caf6d009cacaf8b13bfc58a3e0eadbbdfd7aab01fb0d4154f476.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2y-3\\le x\\le -{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y-3}^{-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363098 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363099 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363100 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363101 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363102 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363099 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363097 1080 #uuid "ec70df83-3cc5-54d5-84b9-e21b1cbe078e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363098 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{2y-3}^{1}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363098 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363098 1084 #uuid "e34dcd5c-c548-555f-9d01-08b2082ee6b5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363099 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y-3}^{-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363099 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363099 1084 #uuid "e18f17c5-7c1e-57f7-8c6c-914f7ad84ff8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363100 1081 "{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y-3}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363100 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363100 1084 #uuid "92f50e5a-02c5-577c-aef6-8553b78e20a0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363101 1081 "{\\int }_{2y-3}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363101 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363101 1084 #uuid "02529dfd-091f-5dfe-8f9c-f37ba8ceaee6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363102 1081 "{\\int }_{2y-3}^{-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363102 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363102 1084 #uuid "eeb3ceb7-f1b3-5f08-8d14-04c619324de8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363103 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363104 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363103 1069 "q-132561" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363103 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363103 1071 "![](images/4d/4de0680e2b6f29892a44fb114653e01433519ae01401d528a1e0263d6577003b.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}3y\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5$ and $y=2x,$ above the $x$-axis, as shown in the picture." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363103 1072 #uuid "5628c3f3-db95-5237-8eb0-cd87e11d0c06" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363103 1074 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}} \\\\ y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ 5-{y}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ 20-4{y}^{2} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ 5{y}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/db/db2d8b0a039490c1065fdb55771f47d36da4b6480e398b8bf8aea952fc2e8012.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}3y\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}}3y\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}}3y\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3y[{\\int }_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3y[x]_{y/2}^{\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3y(\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}y)dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3y\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3y\\sqrt{5-{y}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2})dy & ={[-(5-{y}^{2})^{3/2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1-4)-(-5\\sqrt{5}-0)) \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363105 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363106 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363107 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363108 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363104 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363109 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363104 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363104 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true