17592186363215 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $-3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363215 1072 #uuid "1896da03-9822-50e1-8935-797efb12d1b2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363215 1074 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =-3[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement I is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363217 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363218 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363219 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363220 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363216 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363221 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363216 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 1