074 "First, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is odd and it is an odd number\" to just \"$x$ is odd.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is odd, or $x$ is odd or it is a prime number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$x$ is odd or $x$ is odd, or it is a prime number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is odd or $x$ is odd\" to just \"$x$ is odd.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is odd, or it is a prime number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$x$ is odd or prime.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363460 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363461 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363462 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363463 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363464 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363460 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363459 1080 #uuid "b7fa6fd1-c852-5ca2-8111-31391b68c5a6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363460 1081 "$x$ is odd or prime." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363460 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363460 1084 #uuid "f5dce47e-44d3-5a2b-8197-8bc58ccfa8f6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363461 1081 "$x$ is odd or prime but not both." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363461 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363461 1084 #uuid "927712c1-5e63-55f4-b93d-ce9a38637890" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363462 1081 "$x$ is odd." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363462 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363462 1084 #uuid "b24ed5bb-b839-5d04-9f01-99bfbc097da7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363463 1081 "$x$ is prime." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363463 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363463 1084 #uuid "ad5492ea-f705-5e32-8c74-2af730823972" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363464 1081 "$x$ is odd and prime." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363464 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363464 1084 #uuid "fad267b6-504e-5fd0-b9ce-01ef1a3a6d5b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363465 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363466 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363465 1069 "q-171076" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363465 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363465 1071 "Identify the sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is rational, and $x$ is positive and it is rational.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363465 1072 #uuid "3f6e3428-041f-5cbf-ae7f-ce6c0ed128b1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363465 1074 "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is positive and it is rational\" with the phrase \"$x$ is rational and it is positive.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and $x$ is rational and it is positive.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational, and it is positive.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational\" to just \"$x$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and it is positive.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and positive.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363467 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363468 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363469 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363470 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363471 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363471 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363466 1080 #uuid "dd0feffb-4b11-5a56-bef2-5aa86e59c479" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363467 1081 "$x$ is rational but not positive" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363467 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363467 1084 #uuid "a2d2babc-0a52-545a-96fe-97d822357d85" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363468 1081 "$x$ is rational or positive" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363468 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363468 1084 #uuid "59a40c19-b843-58ac-acb1-3bbbb21d8b37" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363469 1081 "$x$ is rational" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363469 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363469 1084 #uuid "8e6b17e4-5858-554e-bc46-b6c212c5dc6f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363470 1081 "$x$ is not rational nor positive" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363470 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363470 1084 #uuid "64b3f518-577d-50ff-8012-1cda6af9348b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363471 1081 "$x$ is rational and positive" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363471 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363471 1084 #uuid "10ecd84c-a7df-58e0-9133-e1e2560cbf28" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363472 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363473 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363472 1069 "q-171077" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363472 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363472 1071 "Identify the sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is prime, or $x$ is composite or it is prime.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363472 1072 #uuid "176d31fb-490e-5567-b315-c8c4fe6f5140" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363472 1074 "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is composite or it is prime\" with the phrase \"$x$ is prime or it is composite.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is prime, or $x$ is prime or it is composite.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is prime or $x$ is prime, or it is composite.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is prime or $x$ is prime\" to just \"$x$ is prime.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is prime, or it is composite.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is prime or composite.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363474 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363475 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363476 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363477 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363478 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363477 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363473 1080 #uuid "ffa6d06f-981d-5540-b8a8-ead503478c3a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363474 1081 "$x$ is not prime nor composite" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363474 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363474 1084 #uuid "45aea04f-f473-562e-b157-75f5cf902814" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363475 1081 "$x$ is prime but not composite" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363475 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363475 1084 #uuid "20f60ca1-9e9d-537a-aad2-97892c37ea2a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363476 1081 "$x$ is prime and composite" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363476 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363476 1084 #uuid "f2a0759c-8531-58ac-9b56-cf4965e982b2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363477 1081 "$x$ is prime or composite" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363477 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363477 1084 #uuid "d8e2b98e-0bee-53c8-82d3-90778e844863" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363478 1081 "$x$ is prime" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363478 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363478 1084 #uuid "4f2abbd8-93cd-52cc-a81d-f688fa3a33a6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363480 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1069 "q-171678" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1071 "![](images/be/bedd89f5d2804ee3880e6b07483043b61681e73b5d2b04a8d1487c8fd8b225ca.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of the predicates $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P∨Q?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1072 #uuid "29225bf4-a376-5ce0-9264-a0534870eb8d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363479 1074 "The truth set of $P∨Q$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∨Q}={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x,y)∨Q(x,y),$ we take all