n take $n=3.$ And so on. In general, it's sufficient to take $n=m+1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,m\\in N,\\,∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀\\,m\\in N\\,(\\,{{∃n\\in N,\\,m\\le n}_{⏟}}_{P(m)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(m)$ is true over the universal set $N.$ And, according to statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363525 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363526 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363527 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363528 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363529 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363525 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363524 1080 #uuid "f4fae91b-ea7b-504e-9ef4-a13632f1541b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363525 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363525 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363525 1084 #uuid "6661bac9-191c-5925-93f4-bb505689a14f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363526 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363526 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363526 1084 #uuid "664176c4-a482-595a-b227-7a54d76b9b54" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363527 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363527 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363527 1084 #uuid "1965617d-32bf-5547-83e4-c0e97da92b5d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186