 \"every\" indicates we should use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The sentence refers to integers. So, by denoting an integer number as $x,$ we have that \n\n$$\n∀\\,x\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as \n\n$$\nx\\text{ is even or }x\\text{ is odd}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows: \n\n$∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x$ is even or $x$ is odd." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363539 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363540 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363541 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363542 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363543 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363540 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363538 1080 #uuid "4d83af95-1f21-549d-8397-386235b256d5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1081 "$∃\\,x\\in R,\\,x$ is even or $x$ is odd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1084 #uuid "31fc5505-93fc-526b-8a2f-cbbde7f271e0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363540 1081 "$∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x$ is even or $x$ is odd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363540 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363540 1084 #uuid "6c9ce252-09c7-5e9f-8e60-b06e38e2377f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363541 1081 "$∃\\,x,y\\in Z,\\,x$ is even or $y$ is odd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363541 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363541 1084 #uuid "9352bb14-a053-57c1-abc0-1b01b399b6e0" 13194139533445 1759