620 1074 "The truth set of $P(x)∧Q(x)$ represents the *intersection* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∧Q}={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of all even positive integers, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={2,4,6,8,10,…}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}={1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∧Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8,10,…}\\cap {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8} \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363622 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363623 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363624 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363625 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363626 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363625 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363621 1080 #uuid "b6008530-c5b5-5acd-9712-ba33e3118418" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363622 1081 "{2,4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363622 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363622 1084 #uuid "c3d06497-32e7-58ab-83a0-75f2135f61a2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363623 1081 "{1,3,5,7}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363623 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363623 1084 #uuid "a2d4249d-f682-5902-a6ee-ad0700b412da" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363624 1081 "{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363624 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363624 1084 #uuid "0b1923bb-4b69-5756-9b68-893c0a2d6419" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363625 1081 "{2,4,6,8}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363625 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363625 1084 #uuid "45c0a44d-5a39-533b-8d02-20513963bcbd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363626 1081 "{8}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363626 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363626 1084 #uuid "86299578-1dfb-5e8d-9bf7-f1be9841a7ac" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363627 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363628 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363627 1069 "q-176046" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363627 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363627 1071 "$\\,$ $2∣x$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363627 1072 #uuid "f75df828-347b-54cf-9045-e00fd852e459" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363627 1074 "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $2$ divides $x.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $2$ divides $x$, \n\nIn other words, $2$ does not divide $x.$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $2∤x$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363629 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363630 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363631 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363632 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363633 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363631 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363628 1080 #uuid "a832557e-5a57-5ba9-af2d-238b75d90986" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363629 1081 "2∣x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363629 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363629 1084 #uuid "b73feab6-fd57-54c0-82f0-b867514070fb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363630 1081 "x∤2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363630 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363630 1084 #uuid "aa73d7e5-c33f-5ff9-9b0b-ccc7f4e9a262" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363631 1081 "2∤x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363631 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363631 1084 #uuid "1487635a-91a2-5914-ac86-790e71c2479f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363632 1081 "x∣2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363632 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363632 1084 #uuid "58c4f7cc-152d-5d7a-b2dc-5aff1db00c69" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363633 1081 "-x∤-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363633 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363633 1084 #uuid "b819a34f-9443-52e8-b624-0b4f3c7b15e9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363634 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363635 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363634 1069 "q-176845" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363634 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363634 1071 "$\\,$ $x\\ne \\sqrt{2}$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363634 1072 #uuid "d1939292-db35-52a4-92a2-50613c717398" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363634 1074 "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not equal to $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is not equal to $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *equal to* $\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363636 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363637 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363638 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363639 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363640 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363637 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363635 1080 #uuid "2fa26118-7855-5bfb-9804-f776fc88ba4e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363636 1081 "x\\ne -\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363636 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363636 1084 #uuid "1e94dab6-2afe-5d65-8d99-062ef761148c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363637 1081 "x=\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363637 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363637 1084 #uuid "87bd809b-103a-53a7-8cb0-6f4b40dff6bd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363638 1081 "x\\ne \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363638 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363638 1084 #uuid "a2922dcd-b91a-59b9-a