0ade3b9d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363741 1074 "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in {3,7}.$\n\n- $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ is equivalent to $x\\in {3,7}.$\n\n- If $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ then $x\\in {3,7},$ and if $x\\in {3,7}$ then $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363743 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363744 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363745 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363746 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363747 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363747 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363742 1080 #uuid "fdc97073-4b1c-5916-9f40-170a84490dd3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363743 1084 #uuid "209d2bd5-6761-5c94-ba92-88b5074ca51b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363744 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363744 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363744 1084 #uuid "199c8724-565e-5dce-ad7e-bfa2f74b7250" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363745 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363745 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 1759218