915 1069 "q-216487" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363915 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363915 1071 "$\\,$ $I(m):$ ${3}^{m}$ is prime\n\nGiven the predicate above, which of the following expresses the statement $∃m\\in N,\\,I(m)?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363915 1072 #uuid "98b1b177-adec-5faf-ab81-f40bace64cae" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363915 1074 "The existential quantifier \"$∃$\" means \"there exists.\" So, the statement \n$∃m\\in N,\\,I(m)$ \nreads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $m\\in N$ **such that** ${3}^{m}$ is prime.\n\n**Note:** This statement is true because ${3}^{1}=3$ is a prime number." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363917 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363918 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363919 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363920 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363921 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363921 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363916 1080 #uuid "30844bba-5ccd-5425-8a88-19442f199fae" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363917 1081 "There exists a prime number $m\\in N$ such that ${3}^{m}\\in N.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363917 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363917 1084 #uuid "4b57787d-3392-5aa0-867a-d55f21f43fc7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363918 1081 "For all $m\\in N,\\,{3}^{m}$ is not prime." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363918 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363918 1084 #uuid "44cbe000-47b4-5fef-b336-f3c78cbdbad8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1081 "For all $m\\in N,\\,{3}^{m}$ is prime." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1084 #uuid "1d0b64e5-f73e-5d5e-a5ab-4280e4cfcb44" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363920 1081 "For all prime numbers $m\\in N,\\,{3}^{m}\\in N.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363920 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363920 1084 #uuid "d9aab805-3bba-5c46-8870-be56d4f35bd2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363921 1081 "There exists $m\\in N$ such that ${3}^{m}$ is prime." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363921 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363921 1084 #uuid "2abb3656-11e9-5c89-b228-173a8f8daa14" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363923 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1069 "q-216492" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1071 "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $2x+1=0$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$\n- $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1072 #uuid "a35352a2-6307-508d-9bf3-f6a84812f3f7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1074 "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the solution of the equation $2x+1=0$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ but this solution doesn't belong to the universal set. Therefore, the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=∅.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement II is false.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ is empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363924 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363925 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363926 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363927 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363928 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363925 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1080 #uuid "d5a147db-56a8-50cd-983c-49933ef4cc27" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1084 #uuid "9170f417-3243-5e47-afc3-cb7625e69ced" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1084 #uuid "780c2a19-38fd-51db-8977-e14b43049e9f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363926 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363926 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363926 1084 #uuid "566a406d-61f6-5ded-87f0-5351bdc56203" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363927 1081 "None of the statements are true." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363927 1084 #uuid "dd8655cd-b11a-5ceb-aa68-03293daf3557" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363928 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363928 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363928 1084 #uuid "39a7b5b2-e69b-5724-95ec-fa51562eb370" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363929 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363930 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363929 1069 "q-216493" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363929 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363929 1071 "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x<1$ and $|x|\\ge 1.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $R,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is $R.$\n- $∃x\\in R,\\,P(x).$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363929 1072 #uuid "ac3fd956-3cf4-5e15-bb4c-d8f2d84edef6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363929 1074 "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$x<1$\" is $(-\\infty ,1),$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"$|x|\\ge 1$\" is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,1)\\cap ((-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ))=(-\\infty ,-1].\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, ${T}_{P}\\ne R.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is not empty, the statement $∃x\\in R,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363931 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363932 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363933 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363934 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363935 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363934 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363930 1080 #uuid "21afa244-6a93-5a8a-9597-772c7d08c893" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363931 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363931 1084 #uuid "1fda3074-4966-5380-8de9-8e357bb0691a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363932 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363932 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363932 1084 #uuid "87700405-1bdd-5507-9bfb-bda18ce77b2a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363933 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363933 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363933 1084 #uuid "1482e22c-1b3d-55d1-b466-35b58d6d2db4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363934 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363934 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363934 1084 #uuid "9b3cba60-b326-5060-b09d-ee2688ace2a2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363935 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1