begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and the $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{1}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get ${x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{1}=1,$ we get the eigenvector\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364123 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364124 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364125 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364126 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364127 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364124 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364122 1080 #uuid "23debfe4-2fd4-51fd-9d68-368fe9abe15c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364123 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364123 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364123 1084 #uuid "52b796c7-4b43-5d94-8010-87879b0e4f08" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364124 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364124 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364124 1084