e point $(-1,1).$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364193 1072 #uuid "684028b0-fca2-5e81-bf94-98e01d24397f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364193 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}+{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the chain rule and constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2})+{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3})+{e}^{xy}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+{e}^{xy}\\cdot y\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+y{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(-1,1)} & =3(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+(1){e}^{(-1)(1)} \\\\  & =3+{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364195 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364196 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364197 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364198 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364199 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364196 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364194 1080 #uuid "96d9e209-65c0-591c-9c57-813c74680ed7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364195 1081 "1+e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364195 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364195