true] [17592186364269 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xy),$ find the set of values $(x,y)$ on which $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ exists." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1072 #uuid "4dd0e620-fdf6-56fb-b1ff-11292db39e41" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364269 1074 "First, notice that $f(x,y)$ is defined when $-1\\le xy\\le 1.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le xy\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(xy)^{2}}}\\cdot x \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ is defined only for \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}{y}^{2} & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2}{y}^{2} & <1 \\\\ -1<xy & <1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n So, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1<xy<1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le xy\\le 1}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,-1<xy<1} \\\\  & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1<xy<1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364271 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364272 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364273 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364274 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364275 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364273 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364270 1080 #uuid "128389e5-4c10-54a7-ab3a-691a2d7a80e7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364271 1081 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy<1}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364271 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364271 1084 #uuid "a3db0e4a-dd3c-5de5-ab23-3261055f45f1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364272 1081 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy\\ne 1}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364272 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364272 1084 #uuid "2f33740b-6c0d-5ba8-b89d-65acd82ecaf2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364273 1081 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1<xy<1}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364273 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364273 1084 #uuid "a866d36a-0e2e-5905-85e5-0770843c0def" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364274 1081 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le xy\\le 1}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364274 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364274 1084 #uuid "77f32343-615a-517d-a21c-43ae82b960b5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1081 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>1}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364275 1084 #uuid "21f0c51b-ed26-5bae-a3ce-18bedb1e0e61" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364277 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1069 "q-72007" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1071 "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{z}$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{y{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2z\\sqrt{xy}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2z\\sqrt{xy}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y,z)$ on which all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1072 #uuid "07b7a4d5-0d88-5759-b677-08d7e8ac3fca" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364276 1074 "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{z}$ is defined only when $xy\\ge 0$ and $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}=\\frac{y{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2z\\sqrt{xy}}$ is defined only when $xy>0$ and $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domain of ${f}_{y}=\\frac{x{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2z\\sqrt{xy}}$ is the same\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\n- The function ${f}_{z}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{{z}^{2}}$ is defined only when $xy\\ge 0$ and $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{z}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{z}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364278 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364279 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364280 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364281 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364282 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364279 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364277 1080 #uuid "bb805034-5a71-5881-8d6e-dc2faac4f6f6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364278 1081 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z>0}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364278 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364278 1084 #uuid "7f815155-04df-505a-b90c-02233f925ad7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364279 1081 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>0,z\\ne 0}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364279 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364279 1084 #uuid "a251a802-17c8-5538-b07d-0284f94244c1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364280 1081 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0,z\\ne 0}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364280 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364280 1084 #uuid "a45af148-f324-5595-94fb-d8a75c7d31ff" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364281 1081 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ne 0,z<0}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364281 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364281 1084 #uuid "b4615464-f44d-598c-81f7-059882147bf6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1081 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy=0,z\\ne 0}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364282 1084 #uuid "c532f18e-2b4d-55ec-8919-7a91f96a1f01" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364284 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1069 "q-72011" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}?$\n\n- ${f}_{y}(1,-1)$ is defined\n- Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,0)$\n- ${f}_{x}(1,1)$ is defined" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1072 #uuid "fa8a43bb-df08-5eee-88ea-f9abcdd2fb8a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364283 1074 "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}\\cdot \\frac{-1}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}}{2\\sqrt{x-y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,-1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}={e}^{\\sqrt{2}},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,-1)=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{2}}}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,0)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,0)={e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}={e}^{1}=e,\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,0) & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}}{2\\sqrt{1-0}}=\\frac{{e}^{1}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{e}{2} \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,0) & =-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}}{2\\sqrt{1-0}}=-\\frac{{e}^{1}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=-\\frac{e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we substitute $(1,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(1,1)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-1}}}{2\\sqrt{1-1}}=\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{0}}=\\frac{1}{0}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I and II  only'." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364285 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364286 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364287 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364288 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364289 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364288 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364284 1080 #uuid "8c517d13-4ce6-527a-b3ce-ca2edcfc9904" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364285 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364285 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364285 1084 #uuid "1e570ff9-ba40-51a6-b10f-3e8b4b8a1efc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364286 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364286 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364286 1084 #uuid "96ff9ddf-e7f3-5cb7-a289-9f327d912d8a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364287 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364287 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364287 1084 #uuid "5e4439ab-e45c-5c5c-a37e-64c3b1f4c2d2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364288 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364288 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364288 1084 #uuid "4eab8f87-78e7-5b92-8311-4b200cac830b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364289 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364289 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364289 1084 #uuid "b8ea48c5-1f06-568b-b1c8-d61be82ec911" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364290 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364291 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364290 1069 "q-72019" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364290 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364290 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2x+y-z}?$ \n\n- ${f}_{y}(1,1,1)$ is defined\n- ${f}_{z}(0,1,2)$ is defined\n- The partial derivative with respect to $x$ is defined at $(0,1,1)$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364290 1072 #uuid "ff98942c-b72f-558c-86fd-786f6575a16d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364290 1074 "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+y-z}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,1,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,1,1)=\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+1-1}=\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,1,1) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+1-1}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. If we substitute $(0,1,2)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(0,1,2)=\\sqrt{2\\cdot 0+1-2}=\\sqrt{-1},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since the number under the radical is negative.\n\n- Statement III is false. If we substitute $(0,1,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(0,1,1)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 0+1-1}}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I only'." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364292 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364293 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364294 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364295 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364296 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364294 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364291 1080 #uuid "c50da896-45b8-57cb-91f7-c47a8