 $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the lowest $y$-value is $1,$ and it occurs at the point $(2,1).$ The graph will cover all $y$-values from $y=1$ and greater, including the number $1,$ so the range of the function is $[1,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is false. Consider $y=0.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364374 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364375 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364376 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364377 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364378 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364374 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364373 1080 #uuid "15d3aee5-3411-5e5b-a9b3-ddf811b3fb50" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364374 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364374 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364374 1084 #uuid "3e368e3d-df6c-5430-aa33-91580dba6ec1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364375 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364375 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364375 1084 #uuid 