e plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=-1 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1+0\\cdot x-1\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+0\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364575 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364576 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364577 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364578 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364579 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364575 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364574 1080 #uuid "4019a2e8-a359-5366-bd38-fdd0cead739f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364575 1081 "1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364575 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364575 1084 #uuid "6d1a3435-60