ws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns ($1$st and $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a-b=1-1=0.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364623 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364624 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364625 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364626 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364627 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364627 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364622 1080 #uuid "db6e6cfe-224b-582d-a339-40b97c0e9678" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364623 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364623 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364623 1084 #uuid "f6f6a680-345d-5a5b-99e4-e6fe2833a541" 13194139533445 17592186045