1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364649 1072 #uuid "81d378b2-231c-5d07-922f-4a8c686008d2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364649 1074 "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}14 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364651 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364652 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364653 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364654 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364655 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364655 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364650 1080 #uuid "240379d3-c0ac-56d8-a1b8-814d27c2a6bf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364651 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364651 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364651 1084 #uuid "843b36fc-a979-5d98-9172-f5a5e36f6eeb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364652 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364652 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364652 1084 #uuid "8c4c364f-8b3a-59b9-a62e-1632ec0c6c9a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364653 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364653 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364653 1084 #uuid "6f2f6a7d-f3f7-59c9-83c7-88653f472779" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364654 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364654 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364654 1084 #uuid "e70b3f15-2b72-556d-8d3d-7217fc758d42" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364655 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364655 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364655 1084 #uuid "de07c50e-35f1-5988-87f3-73d189220c4c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364656 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364657 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364656 1069 "q-88690" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364656 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364656 1071 "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-5}^{5}2{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}3{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364656 1072 #uuid "4956b231-c3b6-599c-b16a-8affdf879701" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364656 1074 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=2{x}^{4}$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =2(-x)^{4} \\\\  & =2{x}^{4} \\\\  & \\ne -f(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(-x)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $f(x)=3{e}^{-x}$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =3{e}^{-(-x)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{x} \\\\  & \\ne -f(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364658 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364659 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364660 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364661 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364662 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364662 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364657 1080 #uuid "ef6621e0-c427-56b2-83eb-63369faf21de" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364658 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364658 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364658 1084 #uuid "e5f4672d-609d-59d3-a71d-75dd91adda6a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364659 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364659 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364659 1084 #uuid "25073dcd-b946-53a0-911a-0a173ac1ec1d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364660 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364660 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364660 1084 #uuid "5da805df-01ed-5ef1-b851-b8f81e65b003" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364661 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364661 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364661 1084 #uuid "4d1af657-2cb6-5b0b-9c3a-3ab790f5e641" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364662 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364662 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364662 1084 #uuid "5cbb53f5-8c26-510c-9179-16628ebd61e5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364663 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364664 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364663 1069 "q-89550" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364663 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364663 1071 "![](images/d6/d6f00e63a577dff29021e50add69cf916b3f74ed90530b5f4c9f46295950b416.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{x}^{3}\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ above the $x$-axis, as shown in the picture." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364663 1072 #uuid "f13b8b49-8217-594e-a1e7-695fd01b0cfe" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364663 1074 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}} & =\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =4-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =16-4{y}^{2} \\\\ 3{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/ec/ec8853d64b58c40935b769745d5adb9ebc5c84b7f9407cc93dff4b809ed64ad5.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{x}^{3}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,{x}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,{x}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,{x}^{3}\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,{[\\,\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}\\,]}_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\text{ }dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\frac{1}{4}[{(4-{y}^{2})}^{2}-{(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4})}^{2}]dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,[(16-8{y}^{2}+{y}^{4})-(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{16})]dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,(15-\\frac{15}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{15}{16}{y}^{4})dy \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{16})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{16})dy & =\\frac{15}{4}{[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{80}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}[(2-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{2}{5})-0] \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364665 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364666 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364667 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364668 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364669 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364667 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364664 1080 #uuid "95f530d4-be17-5a5f-8b00-55f168260743" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364665 1081 "\\frac{4}{15}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364665 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364665 1084 #uuid "b861f489-607a-54e8-8be4-cd68a12b910f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364666 1081 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364666 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364666 1084 #uuid "37b0d41c-cbf1-5780-8fe1-3886e27f1e49" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364667 1081 "4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364667 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364667 1084 #uuid "23e016f9-01a7-5cfe-a9e8-d9d18a841e54" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364668 1081 "\\frac{16}{15}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364668 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364668 1084 #uuid "95653e8c-81ec-5a74-9311-122bc157256b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364669 1081 "\\frac{15}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364669 