ormation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ to the origin. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$\n- $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- $\\text{rank}(T)=0$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364717 1072 #uuid "5aa9ee11-e88d-5123-8f62-331a18227a4a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364717 1074 "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is the zero-subspace ${0},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=0\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have that\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364719 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364720 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364721 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364722 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364723 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364722 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364718 1080 #uuid "88120105-88c0-5a0f-83b3-a2d57b04464b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364719 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364719 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1